<title>GERMANY: Viag expects sales of 60 bln marks by 2000.</title>
<headline>Viag expects sales of 60 bln marks by 2000.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The chief executive of German diversified utility VIAG AG said on Friday that he expected the company to have sales of 60 billion marks by the year 2000 and wanted to raise profits further after 1997.</p>
<p>&quot;By the turn of the century I expect Viag to have sales of the order of 60 million marks,&quot; Obermeier told Reuters.</p>
<p>Earlier Viag reported sales of 42.5 billion marks for 1996, up from 41.9 billion marks in 1995.</p>
<p>Operating profit before tax in 1996 rose to just under 2.4 billion marks from 2.1 billion marks, Viag said.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
